# The RECEIVE walk: what assets/receive.gif is a recording of. It needs the
# customized image — the RECEIVE build from 'make fw-receive', which carries
# the amp envelope whose trigs shape the machine's volume — and starts from
# the out/fx fixture, the same set and empty project the demo walk uses:
#
#   the machine list, where RECEIVE stands in NEIGHBOR's slot
#   SRC1 and SRC2 pointed at tracks 2 and 3
#   LV1 and LV2 turned up together, so both tracks reach the mix
#   record mode, every one of the sixteen steps at once, and a bar of it
#
# Record it with:
#   make receive-gif        (builds the fixture and the image it needs)
#
# ☠ RECEIVE is on TRACK 1 deliberately. Stock NEIGHBOR refuses tracks 1 and 5,
# having no predecessor inside a DSP core's group of four; RECEIVE running
# there is the whole point of the machine, so the film shows it there.
#
# ☠ Waits are in GUEST time (wait_guest_ms), not wall time. The emulator does
# not hold realtime on a busy host — measured at load average 121, 52 s of
# wall-clock waits gave the guest 5.0 s of audio and every gesture landed in
# an Octatrack that had barely booted.
#
# ☠ Nothing here is saved; tests/walks/demo.jsonl says why at length. Unlike
# that walk, this one holds the recording shut until the machine is up: the
# splash is already in the other film and does not need showing twice.
{"record":0}
{"wait_text":"PTCH","timeout_ms":180000}
# ☠ Not a settle: the firmware is still reading the set off the card behind
# that dialog, and driving the panel before it closes loses keys.
{"wait_gone":"L0ADING FILE5","timeout_ms":60000}
{"wait_guest_ms":1500}
{"record":1}
# FUNC+SRC opens track 1's machine setup, where the list lives.
{"press":"FUNC"}
{"wait_guest_ms":250}
{"tap":"SRC","until":"5RC 5ETUP","verify_ms":20000,"timeout_ms":150000}
{"wait_guest_ms":200}
{"release":"FUNC"}
{"wait_guest_ms":700}
# STATIC, FLEX, THRU, RECEIVE: three down the list, then YES to take it. The
# right-hand half of the page is already RECEIVE's own SRC1..SRC6 by the time
# the cursor lands on it.
{"tap":"DOWN"}
{"wait_guest_ms":350}
{"tap":"DOWN"}
{"wait_guest_ms":350}
{"tap":"DOWN"}
{"wait_guest_ms":500}
{"tap":"YES"}
{"wait_guest_ms":900}
{"mark":"machine"}
# The six slots are the six encoders, A..F, and they are edited HERE, on the
# setup page — the playback page never shows them however many times SRC is
# pressed.
#
# ☠ MEASURED, and twice: a slot moves one track per FOUR detents, not one —
# asking for track 2 with two detents rounds to nothing and the film shows
# OFF. And unlike the level parameters, a selector cares HOW FAST you turn:
# the same eight detents paid out every 87 ms landed on track 1, and every
# 45 ms landed on track 2. So these are eight and twelve detents at the pace
# the measurement was made at, and the film is checked against the screen.
{"encoder":0,"delta":1,"times":8,"over_ms":360,"wait_guest_ms":0}
{"encoder":1,"delta":1,"times":12,"over_ms":540}
{"wait_guest_ms":700}
{"mark":"routed"}
{"tap":"NO","until_gone":"5RC 5ETUP","verify_ms":10000,"timeout_ms":120000}
{"wait_guest_ms":800}
# Back on the playback page, the same six encoders are LV1..LV6 — how much of
# each source reaches the mix. Both hands at once, as a player would.
{"encoder":0,"delta":1,"times":100,"over_ms":2200,"wait_guest_ms":0}
{"encoder":1,"delta":1,"times":100,"over_ms":2200}
{"wait_guest_ms":700}
{"mark":"levels"}
# Grid recording, and then every step at once — both hands flat on the grid,
# not sixteen taps in a row. The presses go out one main-loop pass apart, so
# the keys land inside a quarter of a second and the film reads as one
# gesture.
#
# ☠ The lamp numbers are BIT ids, two to a lamp, so trig N's "a trig lives
# here" bit is 2*(N-1). Only the last one is gated: if step 16 lit, the chord
# was seen, and the walk fails here rather than filming an empty pattern.
{"tap":"REC"}
{"wait_guest_ms":400}
{"press":"TRIG1"}
{"press":"TRIG2"}
{"press":"TRIG3"}
{"press":"TRIG4"}
{"press":"TRIG5"}
{"press":"TRIG6"}
{"press":"TRIG7"}
{"press":"TRIG8"}
{"press":"TRIG9"}
{"press":"TRIG10"}
{"press":"TRIG11"}
{"press":"TRIG12"}
{"press":"TRIG13"}
{"press":"TRIG14"}
{"press":"TRIG15"}
{"press":"TRIG16"}
{"wait_guest_ms":250}
{"release":"TRIG1"}
{"release":"TRIG2"}
{"release":"TRIG3"}
{"release":"TRIG4"}
{"release":"TRIG5"}
{"release":"TRIG6"}
{"release":"TRIG7"}
{"release":"TRIG8"}
{"release":"TRIG9"}
{"release":"TRIG10"}
{"release":"TRIG11"}
{"release":"TRIG12"}
{"release":"TRIG13"}
{"release":"TRIG14"}
{"release":"TRIG15"}
{"release":"TRIG16"}
{"wait_lamp":30,"lit":1,"timeout_ms":20000}
{"wait_guest_ms":600}
{"mark":"trigs"}
# Bit 1 is trig 1's other channel: the playhead crossing step 1, which is the
# evidence the transport actually started. One bar is four beats at the
# project's 120 BPM, so 2000 ms of guest time is the bar.
{"tap":"PLAY","until_lamp":1,"lit":1,"settle_ms":120,"verify_ms":5000,"timeout_ms":120000}
{"wait_guest_ms":2000}
{"panelshot":"out/receive/shot.ppm"}
{"tap":"STOP"}
{"wait_guest_ms":900}
{"mark":"done"}
